{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa: Dinner for Four"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Chewing the Fat"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe routines and regular activities in a wider range of social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le03ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " How much did you use to have?"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " \u201cUsed to\u201d and \u201cwould\u201d express an action that occurred regularly in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use <span class=\"italic\">used to do </span>to talk about the past. It is not a tense but it is like a tense. We use <span class=\"italic\">used to do</span> for the past only.<br /><br /> We use would to describe the pattern of action in the past."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Pattern with used to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Pattern with would\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I used to drink coffee only occasionally.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I would go through about a pound of coffee a month.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Now I go through about a pound of coffee a week,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I used to have about 5 cups of latte a day\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I would go back to the cafe regularly.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Now I only go twice a day.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I used to live on a tight budget.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Back in college, I would save money by making my own coffee.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I still make my own coffee every morning.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Expressing Necessity"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "\u201cHave got to\u201d is used to express necessity.<br />\u201cGoing to have to\u201d expresses a necessary action in the future or a condition."}, {"type": "text", "content": "\u201cHave got to\u201d has irregular forms in the past, present and future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>Present - <span class=\"italic\">I've got to save money.</span></li><li>Past - <span class=\"italic\">I had to live on a tight budget.</span></li><li>Future - <span class=\"italic\">I will have to watch my spending habits.</span></li>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "\"'ve gotta\" is an informal contraction for \"'ve got to\" or \"have go to\".<br/> You use it when you are talking to your friends."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Examples: <br/>  <span class=\"italic\">She'<span class=\"strong\">s gotta</span> find a new hobby.<br/> I'<span class=\"strong\">ve gotta</span> have caffeine.<br/> I'<span class=\"strong\">ve</span> really <span class=\"strong\">gotta</span> cut down on my coffee.<br/> He'<span class=\"strong\">s gotta</span> eat more vegetables.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "\u201cGoing to have to\u201d also expresses a necessary action in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">I'm going have to cut down on my coffee.</span></li><li><span class=\"italic\">I'm going to have to invest in a small machine. </span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "It's also used as a result in a conditional phrase."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">If I'm on a tight budget, I'm going to have to cook more often at home. </span></li></ul>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about eating habits"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "occasionally"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "sometimes or on certain occasions"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I used to drink coffee only occasionally."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to eat out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to eat away from home at a restaurant "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I only eat out once on the weekend."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob09aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to fill up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a phrasal verb to mean fill up a cup, a container or the car's gasoline tank"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Oh, I want more coffee. Fill it up please."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob09aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to cut down"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to reduce in amount "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I've really gotta cut down on my coffee consumption."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob09aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to go through "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to use or consume a certain amount "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I would go through about a pound of coffee a month."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob09aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to invest"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to spend money, time or effort on something that would be valuable for the future"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm going to have to invest in a small cappuccino machine."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob09aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to snack"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to eat a small amount between meals"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can try snacking on some carrot sticks and biscuits. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob09aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think of 3 past eating or drinking habits you used to have. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a sentence about each of them. Use \u201cused to\u201d and \u201cwould\u201d."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Think of 3 current habits you would like to change. Write what you <span class=\"italic\">have got to do to</span> change."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Listen to your partner's ideas and then share yours."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I express past eating habits in writing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I express future necessity in my life in writing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I listen to my partner's ideas."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my ideas verbally with my partner."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about daily routines and eating habits in the past."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express what is necessary."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about quantities and amounts."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you like to eat out for lunch? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": 